# Camp Bus broker ACL (example) — copy to /etc/mosquitto/campbus.acl on the booth Pi.
# Used with bus/mosquitto.conf (allow_anonymous false + password_file). Not used by the
# anonymous dev profile (bus/mosquitto.dev.conf).
#
# Accounts (create each with `mosquitto_passwd /etc/mosquitto/campbus.passwd <name>`):
#   engine   the mapping engine (booth/mapping_engine.py). Routes inputs to cmd/#, applies mapping/set.
#   booth    the booth operator: routes page, camp-mode / vibe controls, game master.
#   audio    the audio analyser / fake_beat: publishes audio/*.
#   bridge   instrument bridges (tools/midi_bridge.py, ESP-NOW-to-MQTT bridge).
#   <node_id>  one account per device (crystal_07, staff_01, matrix_01, ...): username == node_id.
#
# Python services pick their account from CAMPBUS_USER / CAMPBUS_PASSWORD (clients/python/campbus).
#
# Mosquitto checks `user` blocks for the named account and `pattern` lines for everyone
# (%u = username, %c = client id). Anything not granted is denied.

# --- everyone: read the whole bus, publish their own lifecycle / position / input topics
pattern read #
pattern write node/%u/#
pattern write map/%u
pattern write prop/%u
pattern write toy/%u
pattern write instrument/%u

# --- the only accounts allowed to drive devices or rewrite the routing rules
user engine
topic readwrite cmd/#
topic readwrite mapping/#
topic readwrite crystal/#
topic readwrite game/#
topic readwrite display/#
topic readwrite node/#

user booth
topic readwrite cmd/#
topic readwrite mapping/#
topic readwrite camp/#
topic readwrite vibe/#
topic readwrite booth/#
topic readwrite game/#
topic readwrite display/#
topic readwrite config/#
topic readwrite cal/#
topic readwrite kitchen/#
topic readwrite map/#

# --- audio analysis
user audio
topic write audio/#

# --- instrument / prop bridges republish on behalf of many devices
user bridge
topic write instrument/#
topic write prop/#
topic write midi/#
topic write toy/#
